From cf37445a0aa9abcce4b40174ef0a6efdc8225be7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eclipse network tuning <eclipse@localhost>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: stone: enable built-in CAKE for optional tether SQM

Eclipse already contains sch_cake, but stone_defconfig does not enable it.
Build it in so a root module can opt selected egress interfaces into CAKE
without loading an out-of-tree module. Keep the default qdisc unchanged;
rate shaping requires measured rates and explicit opt-in from userspace.

Targets DenBroLiik/eclipse_kernel_xiaomi_stone, seventeen, commit
cf37445a0aa9abcce4b40174ef0a6efdc8225be7 (Linux 5.4).
No modem, firmware, IPA TTL rewrite or RF changes are made.

---
 arch/arm64/configs/stone_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/stone_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/stone_defconfig
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/stone_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/stone_defconfig
@@ -294,6 +294,7 @@
 CONFIG_NET_SCH_INGRESS=y
 CONFIG_NET_SCH_FQ=y
 CONFIG_NET_SCH_FQ_CODEL=y
+CONFIG_NET_SCH_CAKE=y
 CONFIG_NET_CLS_FW=y
 CONFIG_NET_CLS_U32=y
 CONFIG_NET_CLS_BPF=y
-- 
2.43.0
